# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The 1D guide ended by mentioning that local encodings are needed when working with two dimensions. This guide takes that step, for the **two-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard model on a square lattice**, using the **Verstraete-Cirac (VC) encoding** <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18).\n"
msgstr "Panduan 1D berakhir dengan menyebut bahawa pengekodan setempat diperlukan apabila bekerja dengan dua dimensi. Panduan ini mengambil langkah itu, untuk **model Fermi-Hubbard dua dimensi pada kekisi petak**, menggunakan **pengekodan Verstraete-Cirac (VC)** <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are three differences from the 1D problem, forming the basis of this work:\n"
msgstr "Terdapat tiga perbezaan daripada masalah 1D, yang membentuk asas kerja ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The flow sets multiply.** A chain has two arrow orientations; a square lattice has four (east, west, north, south), and each is a union of vertex-disjoint directed paths (one per lattice row or column) rather than a single path.\n"
msgstr "**Set aliran bertambah.** Rantai mempunyai dua orientasi anak panah; kekisi petak mempunyai empat (timur, barat, utara, selatan), dan setiap satu ialah kesatuan laluan berarah yang tidak bersentuhan bucu (satu bagi setiap baris atau lajur kekisi) dan bukan satu laluan tunggal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "## **The encoding gains an ancilla per site**, not one for the whole system, giving a\n"
msgstr "## **Pengekodan memperoleh ancilla bagi setiap tapak**, bukan satu bagi seluruh sistem, memberikan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    qubit-to-mode ratio of $2$. Transfer operators become weight-3 (horizontal) and weight-4 (vertical) Paulis, and each of the four flow sets maps to its own Pauli shape, so each needs its own diagonalizing Clifford.\n"
msgstr "    nisbah qubit-kepada-mod $2$. Operator pindahan menjadi Pauli berat-3 (mengufuk) dan berat-4 (menegak), dan setiap satu daripada empat set aliran dipetakan kepada bentuk Paulinya sendiri, jadi setiap satu memerlukan Clifford pepenjurunya sendiri.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "## **The encoded Hamiltonian is only faithful on a subspace**: the joint $+1$\n"
msgstr "## **Hamiltonian terkod hanya setia pada subruang**: ruang eigen $+1$ bersama\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    eigenspace of the plaquette constraints that every 2D local encoding carries <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19). In 1D the encoding was a plain isometry and the verification was a spectrum check. Here, the comparison has to be projected, as [step 9](#flowsets-2d-stabilizers) illustrates.\n"
msgstr "    kekangan plakuet yang dibawa oleh setiap pengekodan setempat 2D <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19). Dalam 1D pengekodan ialah isometri biasa dan pengesahan ialah semakan spektrum. Di sini, perbandingan mesti diunjurkan, seperti yang digambarkan oleh [langkah 9](#flowsets-2d-stabilizers).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The payoff is the same shape as in 1D: the two-qubit depth of one Trotter step becomes constant in the lattice size, at $24$ ($16$ for the hopping, matching Ref. <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), plus $8$ for the interaction), while a term-by-term Trotterization of the same encoded Hamiltonian grows linearly. The gate count still grows with the number of bonds, of course; what becomes size-independent is how many layers those gates occupy. Depths throughout are counted on an abstract, fully connected register; mapping the encoding onto a device’s restricted coupling map is its own problem, which is discussed at the end.\n"
msgstr "Faedahnya berbentuk sama seperti dalam 1D: kedalaman dua-qubit bagi satu langkah Trotter menjadi malar terhadap saiz kekisi, pada $24$ ($16$ untuk lompatan, sepadan dengan Rujukan <span id=\"id4\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), ditambah $8$ untuk interaksi), manakala penghampiran Trotter sebutan demi sebutan bagi Hamiltonian terkod yang sama bertambah secara linear. Bilangan gate masih bertambah dengan bilangan ikatan, sudah tentu; apa yang menjadi bebas saiz ialah berapa banyak lapisan yang diduduki oleh gate tersebut. Kedalaman sepanjang masa dikira pada daftar abstrak yang bersambung sepenuhnya; memetakan pengekodan ke atas peta gandingan terhad sesuatu peranti ialah masalah tersendiri, yang dibincangkan di akhir.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The lattice and its four orientations {#the-lattice-and-its-four-orientations}"
msgstr "Kekisi dan empat orientasinya {#the-lattice-and-its-four-orientations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first change is visible on the directed interaction graph. Sites are numbered in row-major order, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, and every bond carries both orientations, as the chain did in 1D, but now the bonds run along two axes:\n"
msgstr "Perubahan pertama kelihatan pada graf interaksi berarah. Tapak dinomborkan mengikut tertib baris-utama, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, dan setiap ikatan membawa kedua-dua orientasi, seperti rantai dalam 1D, tetapi kini ikatan berjalan sepanjang dua paksi:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A 3x3 square lattice with both orientations of every horizontal and vertical bond drawn as arrows, the center site carrying all four.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A 3x3 square lattice with both orientations of every horizontal and vertical bond drawn as arrows, the center site carrying all four.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-1.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The commutation rule is the 1D one, unchanged: two transfer operators sharing a site **commute** when the arrows flow through it and **anticommute** when they clash. However, a site now has up to four incident bonds rather than two, so the arrows through it can clash in more ways, and a set of arrows that never clashes is no longer a single path. Reading the horizontal arrows left-to-right gives one such set, the vertical arrows from top-to-bottom gives another, and reversing each gives two more. These are the east, west, north, and south flow sets that organize everything that follows.\n"
msgstr "Peraturan komutasi ialah peraturan 1D, tanpa perubahan: dua operator pindahan yang berkongsi satu tapak **kalis tukar tertib** apabila anak panah mengalir melaluinya dan **antikalis tukar tertib** apabila ia berlanggar. Namun, satu tapak kini mempunyai sehingga empat ikatan bersebelahan dan bukan dua, jadi anak panah melaluinya boleh berlanggar dengan lebih banyak cara, dan set anak panah yang tidak pernah berlanggar bukan lagi satu laluan tunggal. Membaca anak panah mengufuk dari kiri ke kanan memberikan satu set sedemikian, anak panah menegak dari atas ke bawah memberikan satu lagi, dan membalikkan setiap satu memberikan dua lagi. Inilah set aliran timur, barat, utara, dan selatan yang menyusun segala-galanya yang berikut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Verstraete-Cirac encoding {#the-verstraete-cirac-encoding}"
msgstr "Pengekodan Verstraete-Cirac {#the-verstraete-cirac-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verstraete-Cirac (VC) pairs every fermionic mode $j$ with its own auxiliary qubit. With $N$ lattice sites, mode $j$ lives on qubit $j$ and its ancilla is on qubit $N + j$, so the register holds $2N$ qubits. Vertex operators stay as simple as they can be,\n"
msgstr "Verstraete-Cirac (VC) memasangkan setiap mod fermion $j$ dengan qubit tambahannya sendiri. Dengan $N$ tapak kekisi, mod $j$ berada pada qubit $j$ dan ancillanya pada qubit $N + j$, jadi daftar memegang $2N$ qubit. Operator bucu kekal semudah mungkin,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"V_j = Z_j \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which is what makes the occupations directly readable later. Transfer operators depend on the edge orientation. For a horizontal edge $j \\to k$ with $j$ the western site, and a vertical edge with $j$ the northern site,\n"
msgstr "yang menjadikan penghunian boleh dibaca secara langsung kemudian. Operator pindahan bergantung pada orientasi tepi. Bagi tepi mengufuk $j \\to k$ dengan $j$ tapak barat, dan tepi menegak dengan $j$ tapak utara,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{horizontal}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j X_k Z_{N+j} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{vertical}}   = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j Y_k X_{N+j} Y_{N+k} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{horizontal}} = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j X_k Z_{N+j} \\, , \\qquad\n"
"T_{jk}^{\\text{vertical}}   = \\tfrac{1}{2} X_j Y_k X_{N+j} Y_{N+k} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "a weight-3 “triangle” and a weight-4 “square”. Identifying each arrow matters: with $j$ as the western site, $j \\to k$ points east, but with $j$ as the northern site, it points south. The reverse orientations follow from the identity $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, which turns the `XXZ` triangle into `YYZ`, and the `XYXY` square into `YXXY`. Those four distinct labels are the four flow sets, and the rest of this guide tracks them.\n"
msgstr "“segi tiga” berat-3 dan “petak” berat-4. Mengenal pasti setiap anak panah adalah penting: dengan $j$ sebagai tapak barat, $j \\to k$ menunjuk ke timur, tetapi dengan $j$ sebagai tapak utara, ia menunjuk ke selatan. Orientasi songsang diperoleh daripada identiti $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, yang menukarkan segi tiga `XXZ` kepada `YYZ`, dan petak `XYXY` kepada `YXXY`. Empat label berbeza itu ialah empat set aliran, dan selebihnya panduan ini menjejakinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **These are not quite Eq. (A1) of Ref.**   <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), which states “up to single-qubit rotations” and differs in three ways worth naming, since a reader checking the paper will notice:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Ini bukan betul-betul Pers. (A1) dalam Rujukan.**   <span id=\"id5\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), yang menyatakan “sehingga putaran qubit tunggal” dan berbeza dalam tiga perkara yang wajar disebut, kerana pembaca yang menyemak kertas kerja tersebut akan menyedarinya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The prefactor:** Eq. (A1) carries none. The $\\tfrac12$ here is what makes $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac14$, matching the normalization $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a^\\dagger_j - a_j)(a^\\dagger_k + a_k)$ that [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\") uses. The paper only ever needs its transfer operators inside $\\exp(-i\\,dt\\,H)$, where a scale factor is absorbed into the rotation angle; here they have to be *operators* that satisfy an identity.\n"
msgstr "**Faktor pendarab:** Pers. (A1) tidak mempunyainya. $\\tfrac12$ di sini menjadikan $T_{jk}^2 = \\tfrac14$, sepadan dengan normalisasi $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a^\\dagger_j - a_j)(a^\\dagger_k + a_k)$ yang digunakan oleh [`TransferVertexOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator\"). Kertas kerja tersebut hanya memerlukan operator pindahannya di dalam $\\exp(-i\\,dt\\,H)$, yang mana faktor skala diserap ke dalam sudut putaran; di sini ia mestilah *operator* yang memenuhi suatu identiti.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Orientation:** Eq. (A1) selects letters by the row parity of $j$, which for a horizontal edge is the same for both endpoints, so it does not distinguish $T_{jk}$ from $T_{kj}$. The paper recovers the orientation separately, by conjugating with a layer of $R^Z(\\pi/2)$. This guide instead folds it into the encoding, deriving the reverse from $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, which is what makes the two orientations land on different Paulis in step 3.\n"
msgstr "**Orientasi:** Pers. (A1) memilih huruf mengikut pariti baris bagi $j$, yang bagi tepi mendatar adalah sama untuk kedua-dua hujung, jadi ia tidak membezakan $T_{jk}$ daripada $T_{kj}$. Kertas kerja tersebut memulihkan orientasi secara berasingan, dengan mengkonjugasi menggunakan satu lapisan $R^Z(\\pi/2)$. Panduan ini sebaliknya memasukkannya ke dalam pengekodan, dengan memperoleh songsangannya daripada $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$, yang menyebabkan kedua-dua orientasi menghasilkan Pauli yang berbeza dalam langkah 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **The vertical shape:** Eq. (A1) alternates `XXXX` and `YYYY` by row parity, where this guide uses a single `XYXY`. These are two ways of getting the same thing: a letter asymmetry that makes a vertical edge clash correctly with the horizontal edges meeting it. Do not read the difference as a free basis choice. Dropping the parity alternation and using a single `XXXX` breaks the algebra outright, which is why the distinct letters are checked rather than assumed.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Bentuk menegak:** Pers. (A1) berselang-seli antara `XXXX` dan `YYYY` mengikut pariti baris, manakala panduan ini menggunakan satu `XYXY`. Ini ialah dua cara untuk mencapai perkara yang sama: asimetri huruf yang menyebabkan tepi menegak berkonflik dengan betul dengan tepi mendatar yang bertemu dengannya. Jangan anggap perbezaan ini sebagai pilihan asas yang bebas. Membuang selang-seli pariti dan menggunakan satu `XXXX` memusnahkan aljabar sepenuhnya, itulah sebabnya huruf yang berbeza disemak dan bukan diandaikan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The ancilla is attached to a *site*, giving the ratio $2$; it is the Derby-Klassen encoding that places an auxiliary qubit per (odd) plaquette, for the smaller ratio $3/2$. VC is used here because its transfer operators are the ones whose diagonalizing Cliffords Ref.   <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) gives in closed form.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Ancilla dilekatkan pada sebuah *tapak*, memberikan nisbah $2$; pengekodan Derby-Klassen pula meletakkan satu qubit tambahan bagi setiap plakuet (ganjil), untuk nisbah yang lebih kecil iaitu $3/2$. VC digunakan di sini kerana operator pindahannya ialah operator yang Clifford pepenjurunya diberikan dalam bentuk tertutup oleh Rujukan   <span id=\"id6\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. The Hamiltonian on a square lattice {#1-the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice}"
msgstr "1. Hamiltonian pada kekisi segi empat sama {#1-the-hamiltonian-on-a-square-lattice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The construction is the same as in 1D, but with a two-dimensional edge list. Sites keep the row-major numbering used for the figure above, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, so that horizontal bonds connect consecutive indices, and vertical bonds connect indices differing by `cols`:\n"
msgstr "Pembinaannya sama seperti dalam 1D, tetapi dengan senarai tepi dua dimensi. Tapak mengekalkan penomboran utama-baris yang digunakan untuk rajah di atas, `site(r, c) = r * cols + c`, supaya ikatan mendatar menyambungkan indeks berturutan, dan ikatan menegak menyambungkan indeks yang berbeza sebanyak `cols`:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"four-flow-sets-instead-of-two\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Four flow sets instead of two {#2-four-flow-sets-instead-of-two}"
msgstr "2. Empat set aliran dan bukannya dua {#2-four-flow-sets-instead-of-two}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each hopping term is classified by the direction its arrow points on the lattice. Comparing the `divmod` row/column coordinates of the two endpoints separates horizontal from vertical edges, and the sign of the difference picks the orientation. Everything diagonal (the identity, the $V_j$ and the $V_j V_k$ terms) goes into a fifth group:\n"
msgstr "Setiap sebutan lompatan dikelaskan mengikut arah anak panahnya pada kekisi. Membandingkan koordinat baris/lajur `divmod` bagi kedua-dua hujung memisahkan tepi mendatar daripada tepi menegak, dan tanda perbezaan menentukan orientasi. Segala yang pepenjuru (identiti, sebutan $V_j$ dan $V_j V_k$) dimasukkan ke dalam kumpulan kelima:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Orientation convention.** The names are simply read off the figure above: an arrow is **east** or **west** as it points right or left along a row, and **north** or **south** as it points up or down a column. Since the numbering runs row-major, east and south are the index-increasing directions. Nothing downstream depends on the names (they only label groups), but they are easy to confuse, so it is worth fixing them against the picture. Ref.   <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) names its square-lattice flow sets the same way.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Konvensyen orientasi.** Nama-nama itu hanya dibaca daripada rajah di atas: anak panah ialah **timur** atau **barat** apabila ia menuju ke kanan atau kiri sepanjang baris, dan **utara** atau **selatan** apabila ia menuju ke atas atau bawah sepanjang lajur. Memandangkan penomboran berjalan utama-baris, timur dan selatan ialah arah indeks meningkat. Tiada apa-apa di hiliran yang bergantung pada nama tersebut (ia hanya melabel kumpulan), tetapi ia mudah dikelirukan, jadi wajar ditetapkan berdasarkan gambar. Rujukan   <span id=\"id7\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) menamakan set aliran kekisi segi empat samanya dengan cara yang sama.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Within one flow set every arrow either meets another head-to-tail or does not meet it at all, as in 1D, so a flow set still commutes term-by-term and its evolution carries no Trotter error. What is new is that a flow set is now disconnected: the east set of a `rows x cols` lattice consists of `rows` independent left-to-right paths. That disconnection is a gift rather than a complication, as step 6 shows.\n"
msgstr "Dalam satu set aliran, setiap anak panah sama ada bertemu anak panah lain kepala-ke-ekor atau tidak bertemu langsung, seperti dalam 1D, jadi satu set aliran masih kalis tukar tertib sebutan demi sebutan dan evolusinya tidak membawa ralat Trotter. Yang baharu ialah set aliran kini terputus sambungan: set timur bagi kekisi `rows x cols` terdiri daripada `rows` laluan kiri-ke-kanan yang bebas. Keterputusan itu satu kelebihan dan bukannya kerumitan, seperti yang ditunjukkan oleh langkah 6.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"encode-the-operator\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Encode the operator {#3-encode-the-operator}"
msgstr "3. Mengekod operator {#3-encode-the-operator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The encoding is one function that maps a single generalized transfer operator to a Pauli string, which is handed to [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"). Compared with the 1D version, the body has more cases: diagonal, horizontal, vertical, and the reverse orientations through $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$.\n"
msgstr "Pengekodan ialah satu fungsi yang memetakan satu operator pindahan teritlak kepada rentetan Pauli, yang diserahkan kepada [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"). Berbanding versi 1D, badannya mempunyai lebih banyak kes: pepenjuru, mendatar, menegak, dan orientasi songsang melalui $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is one problem. [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") calls back with a generator and nothing else, while deciding a bond’s Pauli string also needs `cols` to recover row and column coordinates from a mode index. Rather than nest the functions to close over it, [`functools.partial()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.partial) binds it, which keeps both functions at the top level and independently callable.\n"
msgstr "Ada satu masalah. [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") memanggil balik dengan sebuah penjana dan tiada yang lain, sedangkan menentukan rentetan Pauli sesuatu ikatan juga memerlukan `cols` untuk memulihkan koordinat baris dan lajur daripada indeks mod. Daripada menyarangkan fungsi untuk menangkapnya, [`functools.partial()`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.partial) mengikatnya, yang mengekalkan kedua-dua fungsi pada peringkat atas dan boleh dipanggil secara bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The point of grouping before mapping can be seen immediately: each flow set encodes to a single Pauli shape, uniform across the whole set.\n"
msgstr "Kelebihan mengumpulkan sebelum memetakan dapat dilihat serta-merta: setiap set aliran dikodkan kepada satu bentuk Pauli, seragam merentasi keseluruhan set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The four hopping shapes are distinct, so each flow set gets its own Clifford in [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis). The reverse orientations are different Paulis, not the same ones relabeled; this is why a 2D flow-set synthesis needs four circuits, where the 1D synthesis needs one.\n"
msgstr "Empat bentuk lompatan itu berbeza, jadi setiap set aliran mendapat Clifford tersendiri dalam [langkah 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis). Orientasi songsang ialah Pauli yang berbeza, bukan yang sama dilabel semula; inilah sebabnya sintesis set aliran 2D memerlukan empat litar, sedangkan sintesis 1D memerlukan satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"transpile-with-the-custom-encoding\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-transpile\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Transpile with the custom encoding {#4-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"
msgstr "4. Transpilasi dengan pengekodan tersuai {#4-transpile-with-the-custom-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This stage is the 1D one with a wider qubit register: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") maps the $N$-mode register onto $2N$ qubits, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") carries the encoding, and its `product_formula` argument selects how the resulting [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) is decomposed. Compare [step 6 of the 1D guide](1-d-fermi-hubbard#flowsets-transpile), which builds the same pipeline for a single ancilla.\n"
msgstr "Peringkat ini ialah peringkat 1D dengan daftar qubit yang lebih lebar: [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") memetakan daftar $N$ mod ke atas $2N$ qubit, [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") membawa pengekodan, dan hujah `product_formula` memilih cara [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) yang terhasil diurai. Bandingkan [langkah 6 panduan 1D](1-d-fermi-hubbard#flowsets-transpile), yang membina saluran paip yang sama untuk satu ancilla.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Five gates, carrying the 6, 6, 6, 6, and 22 terms counted in step 2. Each is mapped and synthesized independently, so the partition decided at the fermionic level survives all the way into the circuit:\n"
msgstr "Lima gate, membawa 6, 6, 6, 6, dan 22 sebutan yang dikira dalam langkah 2. Setiap satu dipetakan dan disintesis secara bebas, jadi pembahagian yang ditentukan pada peringkat fermion kekal sehingga ke dalam litar:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is the baseline: the encoding and the grouping are both in place, but [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) synthesizes each flow set term by term, and the depth grows with the lattice.\n"
msgstr "Itulah garis dasar: pengekodan dan pengumpulan kedua-duanya sudah ada, tetapi [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) mensintesis setiap set aliran sebutan demi sebutan, dan kedalaman bertambah dengan kekisi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. A depth-2 Clifford per flow set {#5-a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set}"
msgstr "5. Clifford berkedalaman 2 bagi setiap set aliran {#5-a-depth-2-clifford-per-flow-set}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The mechanism is the same as in 1D: conjugate a whole commuting flow set by a Clifford that maps each of its terms to a distinct weight-1 Pauli, so that the evolution of the entire set costs only single-qubit rotations. In 1D, one brickwork of `CZ` gates did this.\n"
msgstr "Mekanismenya sama seperti dalam 1D: konjugasikan keseluruhan set aliran yang kalis tukar tertib dengan Clifford yang memetakan setiap sebutannya kepada Pauli berpemberat-1 yang berbeza, supaya evolusi keseluruhan set hanya memerlukan putaran qubit tunggal. Dalam 1D, satu binaan bata `CZ` gate melakukan perkara ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In 2D, each flow set needs its own circuit, following Section IV C and Fig. 7 of Ref. <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17). All four act on one line of the lattice at a time (a row for east/west, a column for north/south) together with that line’s ancillas, and all four have the same three-part shape:\n"
msgstr "Dalam 2D, setiap set aliran memerlukan litarnya sendiri, mengikut Bahagian IV C dan Rajah 7 Rujukan <span id=\"id8\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17). Kesemua empat beroperasi pada satu garisan kekisi pada satu masa (baris untuk timur/barat, lajur untuk utara/selatan) bersama ancilla garisan itu, dan kesemuanya mempunyai bentuk tiga bahagian yang sama:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A layer of single-qubit rotations, putting each qubit in the basis its flow set needs.\n"
msgstr "Satu lapisan putaran qubit tunggal, meletakkan setiap qubit dalam asas yang diperlukan oleh set alirannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A first `CX` layer, always site-to-ancilla on the same site.\n"
msgstr "Lapisan `CX` pertama, sentiasa dari tapak ke ancilla pada tapak yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A second `CX` layer, coupling neighbors along the line.\n"
msgstr "Lapisan `CX` kedua, menggandingkan jiran di sepanjang garisan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 2 and 3 are the only two-qubit layers, so the two-qubit depth is $2$, regardless of how long the line is. They are written out one function per flow set below. The rotations are what they are because they were found, by conjugating each flow set’s terms and requiring distinct weight-1 images, so treat them as given and rely on the check that follows.\n"
msgstr "Langkah 2 dan 3 ialah satu-satunya dua lapisan dua-qubit, jadi kedalaman dua-qubit ialah $2$, tidak kira berapa panjang garisan itu. Ia ditulis satu fungsi bagi setiap set aliran di bawah. Putaran itu sedemikian kerana ia ditemui, dengan mengkonjugasi sebutan setiap set aliran dan menghendaki imej berpemberat-1 yang berbeza, jadi anggaplah ia sebagai diberi dan bergantunglah pada semakan yang menyusul.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two horizontal sets are the simplest. Their terms are weight-3, `XXZ` and `YYZ`, and differ only by the extra $S$ that turns $X$ into $Y$ on the sites:\n"
msgstr "Dua set mendatar ialah yang paling mudah. Sebutannya berpemberat-3, `XXZ` dan `YYZ`, dan hanya berbeza dengan $S$ tambahan yang menukar $X$ kepada $Y$ pada tapak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two vertical sets are weight-4, `XYXY` and `YXXY`, and are correspondingly busier: the rotations alternate with the position along the line, and the second `CX` layer alternates too, coupling sites on even positions and ancillas on odd ones (or the reverse):\n"
msgstr "Dua set menegak berpemberat-4, `XYXY` dan `YXXY`, dan sewajarnya lebih sibuk: putaran berselang-seli mengikut kedudukan di sepanjang garisan, dan lapisan `CX` kedua juga berselang-seli, menggandingkan tapak pada kedudukan genap dan ancilla pada kedudukan ganjil (atau sebaliknya):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Drawn on a single three-site line (its sites first, then their ancillas) the whole mechanism fits in one picture. The triangle shape is the clearer of the two: a basis change on the ancillas, then two `CX` layers, the first pairs each site with its own ancilla and the second reaches to the next site along the line.\n"
msgstr "Dilukis pada satu garisan tiga tapak (tapaknya dahulu, kemudian ancilla mereka), seluruh mekanisme muat dalam satu gambar. Bentuk segi tiga lebih jelas antara kedua-duanya: perubahan asas pada ancilla, kemudian dua lapisan `CX`, yang pertama memasangkan setiap tapak dengan ancillanya sendiri dan yang kedua mencapai tapak seterusnya di sepanjang garisan.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The east Clifford on a three-site line: three H gates on the ancillas followed by two layers of two CX gates each.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The east Clifford on a three-site line: three H gates on the ancillas followed by two layers of two CX gates each.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-11.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The square shape needs more single-qubit work (the rotations alternate along the line) and its second `CX` layer alternates between coupling sites and coupling ancillas:\n"
msgstr "Bentuk segi empat sama memerlukan lebih banyak kerja qubit tunggal (putaran berselang-seli di sepanjang garisan) dan lapisan `CX` keduanya berselang-seli antara menggandingkan tapak dan menggandingkan ancilla:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![The south Clifford on a three-site line: alternating single-qubit rotations followed by two CX layers, the second mixing site-site and ancilla-ancilla pairs.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"
msgstr "![The south Clifford on a three-site line: alternating single-qubit rotations followed by two CX layers, the second mixing site-site and ancilla-ancilla pairs.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-12.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both are two `CX` layers deep, and adding sites to the line widens them without deepening them; that is the whole constant-depth claim, visible by inspection. The west and north Cliffords differ only in their single-qubit layers, so they are not drawn separately.\n"
msgstr "Kedua-duanya berkedalaman dua lapisan `CX`, dan menambah tapak pada garisan melebarkannya tanpa mendalamkannya; itulah keseluruhan dakwaan kedalaman malar, yang nampak melalui pemeriksaan. Clifford barat dan utara hanya berbeza pada lapisan qubit tunggal, jadi ia tidak dilukis secara berasingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the synthesis still needs is determining where each term ends up. A line of $L$ sites carries $L - 1$ bonds, each contributing one term, so the helper below returns one entry per bond: the qubit that the term landed on, and the single-qubit Pauli it became. Crucially, these are read off the conjugation rather than predicted. Unlike 1D, where one `CZ` brickwork maps $X_{j+1} \\mapsto Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}$ in closed form, there is no such formula here, and the ancillas of a column line are not contiguous. The only thing that differs between the flow sets is the Pauli string going in, which step 3 already printed:\n"
msgstr "Apa yang sintesis masih perlukan ialah menentukan ke mana setiap sebutan berakhir. Garisan $L$ tapak membawa $L - 1$ ikatan, masing-masing menyumbang satu sebutan, jadi pembantu di bawah memulangkan satu entri bagi setiap ikatan: qubit tempat sebutan itu mendarat, dan Pauli qubit tunggal yang ia menjadi. Yang penting, ini dibaca daripada konjugasi dan bukan diramal. Tidak seperti 1D, yang mana satu bata `CZ` memetakan $X_{j+1} \\mapsto Z_j X_{j+1} Z_{j+2}$ dalam bentuk tertutup, tiada formula sedemikian di sini, dan ancilla garisan lajur tidak bersebelahan. Satu-satunya perkara yang berbeza antara set aliran ialah rentetan Pauli yang masuk, yang sudah dicetak oleh langkah 3:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The images must come out distinct and weight-1, so that each term can be rotated independently on its own qubit; the two-qubit depth of $2$ is already visible in the four constructions above, each emitting two `CX` layers irrespective of the line length. Below, both properties are checked across every flow set, every line, and several lattice sizes. Step 6 then calls `clifford_supports`, so it is a working part of the synthesis rather than only a demonstration.\n"
msgstr "Imej mesti keluar berbeza dan berpemberat-1, supaya setiap sebutan boleh diputar secara bebas pada qubitnya sendiri; kedalaman dua-qubit $2$ sudah kelihatan dalam empat binaan di atas, masing-masing menghasilkan dua lapisan `CX` tanpa mengira panjang garisan. Di bawah, kedua-dua sifat disemak merentasi setiap set aliran, setiap garisan, dan beberapa saiz kekisi. Langkah 6 kemudian memanggil `clifford_supports`, jadi ia bahagian sintesis yang berfungsi dan bukan sekadar demonstrasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flow-set-aware-synthesis\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Flow-set-aware synthesis {#6-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"
msgstr "6. Sintesis yang peka set aliran {#6-flow-set-aware-synthesis}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The synthesis gets a helpful head start. Because [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") splits itself group by group, `synthesize` is called once per flow set (five times here, four hopping sets plus the diagonal group) so every hopping term it sees shares one Pauli shape, and one Clifford diagonalizes all of them. It only has to read that shape off the first term and sort the rest by which line they sit on. Then comes the observation that makes two dimensions cheaper than one might fear:\n"
msgstr "Sintesis mendapat permulaan yang membantu. Oleh kerana [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") memecahkan dirinya kumpulan demi kumpulan, `synthesize` dipanggil sekali bagi setiap set aliran (lima kali di sini, empat set lompatan ditambah kumpulan pepenjuru) supaya setiap sebutan lompatan yang dilihatnya berkongsi satu bentuk Pauli, dan satu Clifford mendiagonalkan kesemuanya. Ia hanya perlu membaca bentuk itu daripada sebutan pertama dan mengisih yang lain mengikut garisan tempat ia berada. Kemudian datang pemerhatian yang menjadikan dua dimensi lebih murah daripada yang ditakuti:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  The components of a single flow set are vertex-disjoint: the west set’s rows share no qubits. So all of a flow set’s Cliffords can be emitted together and they share the same two two-qubit layers, rather than queueing up one row after another. A flow set therefore costs a fixed number of layers (two for the Clifford and two for its inverse) no matter how many rows or columns the lattice has, which is why the total depth ends up constant.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  Komponen satu set aliran adalah bercerai bucu: baris set barat tidak berkongsi qubit. Jadi semua Clifford sesuatu set aliran boleh dikeluarkan bersama dan berkongsi dua lapisan dua-qubit yang sama, dan bukannya beratur satu baris demi satu baris. Satu set aliran oleh itu menelan bilangan lapisan yang tetap (dua untuk Clifford dan dua untuk songsangannya) tidak kira berapa banyak baris atau lajur kekisi itu, itulah sebabnya jumlah kedalaman akhirnya malar.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As in 1D, this is deliberately written for this encoding: it recognizes the four Pauli shapes and raises on anything else rather than falling back silently. It also assumes the one-flow-set-per-gate split above, and says so; more than one hopping shape in a single gate means the grouping was not applied, which is an error rather than something to work around.\n"
msgstr "Seperti dalam 1D, ini sengaja ditulis untuk pengekodan ini: ia mengenali empat bentuk Pauli dan menimbulkan ralat pada apa-apa yang lain dan bukannya kembali secara senyap. Ia juga mengandaikan pembahagian satu-set-aliran-bagi-setiap-gate di atas, dan menyatakannya; lebih daripada satu bentuk lompatan dalam satu gate bermakna pengumpulan tidak dilaksanakan, yang merupakan ralat dan bukan sesuatu untuk dielakkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Like its 1D counterpart, this synthesis takes no number of Trotter steps. A Trotter step has to cycle *between* the flow sets, but `transpile_trotter_step` below decomposes the fermionic circuit into one [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate per set, so this method only ever sees one set at a time and could only repeat *within* it, which changes nothing: repeating one operator just splits its own evolution into equal pieces.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Seperti rakan 1D-nya, sintesis ini tidak mengambil bilangan langkah Trotter. Satu langkah Trotter perlu berkitar *antara* set aliran, tetapi `transpile_trotter_step` di bawah menguraikan litar fermion kepada satu gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") bagi setiap set, jadi kaedah ini hanya melihat satu set pada satu masa dan hanya boleh mengulang *di dalamnya*, yang tidak mengubah apa-apa: mengulang satu operator hanya membahagikan evolusinya sendiri kepada kepingan yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Multi-step Trotterization therefore needs a product formula that respects the operator’s [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") inside a single gate, before the decomposition. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") does that, and [step 10](#flowsets-2d-convergence) uses it to measure the convergence.\n"
msgstr "  Trotterisasi berbilang langkah oleh itu memerlukan formula hasil darab yang menghormati [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.groups\") operator di dalam satu gate, sebelum penguraian. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") melakukannya, dan [langkah 10](#flowsets-2d-convergence) menggunakannya untuk mengukur penumpuan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Note the two similarly named classes at play. Qiskit’s [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter), used as the baseline above, acts on the *mapped* Hamiltonian, where the grouping is already gone. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") is the fermionic counterpart, and it is the one that can still see the flow sets.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  Perhatikan dua kelas yang bernama serupa di sini. [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) Qiskit, yang digunakan sebagai garis dasar di atas, bertindak pada Hamiltonian yang *dipetakan*, yang pengumpulannya sudah hilang. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") ialah padanan fermionnya, dan ia yang masih dapat melihat set aliran.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"the-result-constant-depth\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. The result: constant depth {#7-the-result-constant-depth}"
msgstr "7. Hasilnya: kedalaman malar {#7-the-result-constant-depth}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Everything so far ran on the single $3 \\times 3$ lattice built in step 1. Comparing the two synthesis paths across growing lattices needs that whole sequence (operator, grouping, encoding, circuit, pass manager) repeated per size, so it is worth wrapping once:\n"
msgstr "Segala-galanya setakat ini dijalankan pada satu kekisi $3 \\times 3$ yang dibina dalam langkah 1. Membandingkan kedua-dua laluan sintesis merentasi kekisi yang membesar memerlukan keseluruhan urutan itu (operator, pengumpulan, pengekodan, litar, pengurus laluan) diulang bagi setiap saiz, jadi wajar dibungkus sekali:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collecting both metrics across a range of lattice sizes and plotting them against the lattice edge makes the difference plain:\n"
msgstr "Mengumpulkan kedua-dua metrik merentasi pelbagai saiz kekisi dan memplotkannya terhadap tepi kekisi menjadikan perbezaannya jelas:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two-qubit depth and CX count against lattice edge; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 24.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-17.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two-qubit depth and CX count against lattice edge; the qubit-level LieTrotter grows linearly while the flow-set synthesis stays flat at 24.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-fermions/2d_fermi_hubbard-17.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two-qubit depth is 24 and constant from $3 \\times 3$ to $8 \\times 8$ (that is 18 qubits up to 128), while [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) applied to the identically encoded Hamiltonian grows linearly with the lattice edge, from 47 to 92. The gate count grows under both, since there are $O(N)$ terms to apply either way; what the flow sets remove is the growth in how many layers those gates occupy.\n"
msgstr "Kedalaman dua-qubit ialah 24 dan malar dari $3 \\times 3$ hingga $8 \\times 8$ (iaitu 18 qubit hingga 128), manakala [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) yang dikenakan pada Hamiltonian berpengekodan serupa bertambah secara linear dengan tepi kekisi, dari 47 kepada 92. Bilangan gate bertambah dalam kedua-duanya, kerana ada $O(N)$ sebutan untuk dikenakan sama ada cara; apa yang dibuang oleh set aliran ialah pertumbuhan bilangan lapisan yang diduduki gate tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The budget splits into 16 for the hopping and eight for the interaction:\n"
msgstr "Belanjawan terbahagi kepada 16 untuk lompatan dan lapan untuk interaksi:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each of the four flow sets costs $2 + 2$ two-qubit layers: its Clifford going in and the inverse coming out, both depth two by construction, with only single-qubit rotations in between. That is $4 \\times 4 = 16$, which is the figure Ref. <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) quotes, since it counts the hopping terms only. Setting $U = 0$ in the code above reproduces it.\n"
msgstr "Setiap satu daripada empat set aliran menelan $2 + 2$ lapisan dua-qubit: Clifford-nya masuk dan songsangannya keluar, kedua-duanya berkedalaman dua mengikut binaan, dengan hanya putaran qubit tunggal di antaranya. Itu ialah $4 \\times 4 = 16$, angka yang dipetik oleh Rujukan <span id=\"id9\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17), kerana ia hanya mengira sebutan lompatan. Menetapkan $U = 0$ dalam kod di atas menghasilkannya semula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagonal group adds the remaining eight. Its `Rzz` gates pack into four layers, and each `Rzz` decomposes into two `CX` gates around a single-qubit rotation, so $4 \\times 2 = 8$. Four layers is optimal: on a square lattice, the interaction reaches only nearest neighbors, so every interior site carries four `Rzz` gates (one per bond) and can take part in only one at a time.\n"
msgstr "Kumpulan pepenjuru menambah lapan yang selebihnya. `Rzz` gate-nya dipadatkan kepada empat lapisan, dan setiap `Rzz` terurai kepada dua gate `CX` mengapit satu putaran qubit tunggal, jadi $4 \\times 2 = 8$. Empat lapisan ialah optimum: pada kekisi segi empat sama, interaksi hanya mencapai jiran terdekat, jadi setiap tapak dalaman membawa empat gate `Rzz` (satu bagi setiap ikatan) dan hanya boleh mengambil bahagian dalam satu pada satu masa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nothing in either sum refers to the lattice size, which is the whole point.\n"
msgstr "Tiada apa-apa dalam kedua-dua jumlah itu merujuk kepada saiz kekisi, dan itulah tujuan keseluruhannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-circuit\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-verify\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Verify the circuit {#8-verify-the-circuit}"
msgstr "8. Sahkan litar {#8-verify-the-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The flow-set synthesis and [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) describe the same Trotter step of the same encoded Hamiltonian, so their unitaries must agree up to a global phase. Random statevectors detect any discrepancy far more cheaply than building the full unitary:\n"
msgstr "Sintesis set aliran dan [`LieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.synthesis.LieTrotter) menghuraikan langkah Trotter yang sama bagi Hamiltonian terkod yang sama, jadi unitarinya mesti sepadan sehingga fasa global. Vektor keadaan rawak mengesan sebarang percanggahan dengan jauh lebih murah daripada membina unitari penuh:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both circuits are decomposed down to one- and two-qubit gates *before* being applied to a state. Left un-decomposed, each high-level `Evolution` instruction forces [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) to build its full $2^{2N} \\times 2^{2N}$ dense operator; decomposing first lets it apply gates one at a time instead, which is several hundred times faster here.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua-dua litar diuraikan kepada gate satu- dan dua-qubit *sebelum* dikenakan pada keadaan. Jika tidak diuraikan, setiap arahan `Evolution` peringkat tinggi memaksa [`Statevector`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Statevector) membina operator tumpat penuh $2^{2N} \\times 2^{2N}$nya; menguraikan dahulu membolehkannya mengenakan gate satu demi satu, yang beratus kali ganda lebih pantas di sini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Both halves of that check matter. A unit-modulus overlap on a single state is necessary but not sufficient: a synthesis that got a state-dependent phase wrong would still show it. Requiring the same phase across several random states is what closes the gap.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Kedua-dua bahagian semakan itu penting. Pertindihan modulus-unit pada satu keadaan adalah perlu tetapi tidak mencukupi: sintesis yang tersalah fasa bergantung keadaan masih akan menunjukkannya. Menghendaki fasa yang sama merentasi beberapa keadaan rawak itulah yang menutup jurang tersebut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-stabilizers\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "9. Verify the physics on the stabilizer subspace {#9-verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace}"
msgstr "9. Sahkan fizik pada subruang penstabil {#9-verify-the-physics-on-the-stabilizer-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is the two-dimensional wrinkle. In 1D, the encoding was an isometry, and comparing spectra against a Jordan-Wigner reference was enough. VC is not an isometry: it uses $2N$ qubits for $N$ modes, so a $2^{2N}$-dimensional space holds a $2^N$-dimensional physical one. This is generic to local encodings in two dimensions (the surplus qubits are constrained by local commuting symmetries, one per plaquette <span id=\"id10\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id11\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19)) and it means the encoded Hamiltonian represents the fermionic one faithfully only on the joint $+1$ eigenspace of those constraints.\n"
msgstr "Inilah kerumitan dua dimensi. Dalam 1D, pengekodan ialah isometri, dan membandingkan spektrum dengan rujukan Jordan-Wigner sudah memadai. VC bukan isometri: ia menggunakan $2N$ qubit untuk $N$ mod, jadi ruang berdimensi $2^{2N}$ memuatkan satu ruang fizikal berdimensi $2^N$. Ini bersifat generik bagi pengekodan setempat dalam dua dimensi (qubit berlebihan dikekang oleh simetri kalis tukar tertib setempat, satu bagi setiap plakuet <span id=\"id10\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18) <span id=\"id11\" />[\\[3\\]](#id19)) dan ia bermakna Hamiltonian terkod mewakili Hamiltonian fermion dengan setia hanya pada ruang eigen $+1$ bersama bagi kekangan tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Warning\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  The word **stabilizer** does double duty in this subject, and the two meanings are unrelated. Ref.   <span id=\"id12\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) uses it for the commuting transfer operators of a flow set, which form a stabilizer group that the Cliffords of [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) diagonalize (a compilation device, and the sense meant everywhere above). This section uses it in the error-correction sense: operators whose $+1$ eigenspace is the physical subspace. Ref.   <span id=\"id13\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) explicitly flags this collision and sets the second meaning aside; the plaquette constraints below are a property of the VC encoding   <span id=\"id14\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18), not a result of the flow-set framework.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Amaran\" type=\"caution\">\n"
"  Perkataan **penstabil** mempunyai dua fungsi dalam bidang ini, dan kedua-dua maknanya tidak berkaitan. Rujukan   <span id=\"id12\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) menggunakannya untuk operator pindahan kalis tukar tertib bagi satu set aliran, yang membentuk kumpulan penstabil yang didiagonalkan oleh Clifford [langkah 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) (alat pengkompilan, dan makna yang dimaksudkan di mana-mana di atas). Bahagian ini menggunakannya dalam erti pembetulan ralat: operator yang ruang eigen $+1}$-nya ialah subruang fizikal. Rujukan   <span id=\"id13\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) menandakan secara jelas pertembungan ini dan mengetepikan makna kedua; kekangan plakuet di bawah ialah sifat pengekodan VC   <span id=\"id14\" />[\\[2\\]](#id18), bukan hasil rangka kerja set aliran.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The generators are constructed here rather than quoted: one per square face, and each is simply the encoded **edge**-operator loop around that face.\n"
msgstr "Penjana dibina di sini dan bukan dipetik: satu bagi setiap muka segi empat sama, dan setiap satu hanyalah gelung operator **tepi** terkod mengelilingi muka itu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Edge operators are the natural object for this. A closed loop of them is a symmetry of any particle-number-conserving Hamiltonian, whereas the corresponding loop of transfer operators is not: the two differ by a vertex operator on each bond’s source site,\n"
msgstr "Operator tepi ialah objek yang wajar untuk ini. Gelung tertutup operator tepi ialah simetri bagi mana-mana Hamiltonian yang memelihara bilangan zarah, manakala gelung operator pindahan yang sepadan bukan: kedua-duanya berbeza dengan operator bucu pada tapak sumber setiap ikatan,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk} = \\tfrac{i}{2} \\, V_j E_{jk}\n"
"\\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad\n"
"E_{jk} = -2i \\, V_j T_{jk} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"T_{jk} = \\tfrac{i}{2} \\, V_j E_{jk}\n"
"\\qquad \\Longleftrightarrow \\qquad\n"
"E_{jk} = -2i \\, V_j T_{jk} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Around a closed loop every site is the source of exactly one bond, so the loop collects one $V_j$ per site, which is the **local parity** of the plaquette’s four sites. That local parity is what makes the difference: the Hamiltonian hops particles across the plaquette boundary, so it conserves only the *global* parity. The bare transfer loop therefore fails to commute with it, while the edge loop (which carries the parity factor) commutes.\n"
msgstr "Mengelilingi gelung tertutup setiap tapak ialah sumber tepat satu ikatan, jadi gelung itu mengumpul satu $V_j$ bagi setiap tapak, iaitu **pariti setempat** bagi empat tapak plakuet. Pariti setempat itulah yang membuat perbezaan: Hamiltonian melompatkan zarah merentasi sempadan plakuet, jadi ia hanya memelihara pariti *global*. Gelung pindahan kosong oleh itu gagal kalis tukar tertib dengannya, manakala gelung tepi (yang membawa faktor pariti) kalis tukar tertib.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since the encoding is defined on transfer operators, mapping an edge operator needs the relation above. That is a five-line callback, and it slots into [`map_edge_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-edge-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators\") exactly as `vc_action` slots into [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"):\n"
msgstr "Memandangkan pengekodan ditakrifkan pada operator pindahan, memetakan operator tepi memerlukan hubungan di atas. Itu ialah panggil balik lima baris, dan ia dimasukkan ke dalam [`map_edge_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-edge-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_edge_vertex_generators\") sama seperti `vc_action` dimasukkan ke dalam [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each generator has weight $6$, spread over two of its plaquette’s physical qubits and four ancillas. They are involutory and commute with the encoded Hamiltonian, so the physical subspace is preserved by the dynamics. Both properties are statements about operators, so they are checked symbolically on the [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) algebra, no $2^{18} \\times 2^{18}$ matrices required:\n"
msgstr "Setiap penjana berpemberat $6$, tersebar pada dua qubit fizikal plakuetnya dan empat ancilla. Ia involutori dan kalis tukar tertib dengan Hamiltonian terkod, jadi subruang fizikal dikekalkan oleh dinamik. Kedua-dua sifat ialah pernyataan tentang operator, jadi ia disemak secara simbolik pada aljabar [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), tanpa memerlukan matriks $2^{18} \\times 2^{18}$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With the stabilizers in hand, the comparison needs no basis correspondence, because $V_j = Z_j$ means the occupations live on the same physical qubits in both pictures. So: write a product state directly on the physical qubits with the ancillas in $|0\\rangle$, project it onto the stabilizer subspace, evolve with the encoded Hamiltonian, and read the site densities $\\langle n_j \\rangle = (1 - \\langle Z_j \\rangle)/2$ off both sides.\n"
msgstr "Dengan penstabil di tangan, perbandingan tidak memerlukan padanan asas, kerana $V_j = Z_j$ bermakna penghunian berada pada qubit fizikal yang sama dalam kedua-dua gambaran. Jadi: tulis keadaan hasil darab terus pada qubit fizikal dengan ancilla dalam $|0\\rangle$, unjurkan ke subruang penstabil, evolusikan dengan Hamiltonian terkod, dan baca ketumpatan tapak $\\langle n_j \\rangle = (1 - \\langle Z_j \\rangle)/2$ daripada kedua-dua belah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every step here stays at the level of a vector. The projector is applied one $(1 + S)/2$ factor at a time instead of being multiplied out, and the time evolution uses [`expm_multiply()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), which computes $e^{-iHt} |\\psi\\rangle$ without ever forming $e^{-iHt}$. Since the encoded Hamiltonian is a sparse $2^{2N}$-dimensional operator, that distinction is what keeps this section cheap.\n"
msgstr "Setiap langkah di sini kekal pada peringkat vektor. Unjuran dikenakan satu faktor $(1 + S)/2$ pada satu masa dan bukan didarabkan sepenuhnya, dan evolusi masa menggunakan [`expm_multiply()`](https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply.html#scipy.sparse.linalg.expm_multiply \"(in SciPy v1.18.0)\"), yang mengira $e^{-iHt} |\\psi\\rangle$ tanpa pernah membentuk $e^{-iHt}$. Oleh kerana Hamiltonian terkod ialah operator jarang berdimensi $2^{2N}$, perbezaan itulah yang menjadikan bahagian ini murah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Those are the encoded densities; they match the Jordan-Wigner reference to machine precision, on a lattice whose encoding is faithful only after projection.\n"
msgstr "Itulah ketumpatan terkod; ia sepadan dengan rujukan Jordan-Wigner sehingga ketepatan mesin, pada kekisi yang pengekodannya setia hanya selepas unjuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"measure-the-trotter-convergence\" />\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"flowsets-2d-convergence\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "10. Measure the Trotter convergence {#10-measure-the-trotter-convergence}"
msgstr "10. Ukur penumpuan Trotter {#10-measure-the-trotter-convergence}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Step 8](#flowsets-2d-verify) established that the two syntheses agree with each other, which is a statement about equivalence rather than accuracy: both describe the same single Trotter step, so both carry the same Trotter error. Measuring that error needs an exact reference, and step 9 just built one.\n"
msgstr "[Langkah 8](#flowsets-2d-verify) menetapkan bahawa kedua-dua sintesis bersetuju antara satu sama lain, yang merupakan pernyataan tentang kesetaraan dan bukan ketepatan: kedua-duanya menghuraikan satu langkah Trotter yang sama, jadi kedua-duanya membawa ralat Trotter yang sama. Mengukur ralat itu memerlukan rujukan tepat, dan langkah 9 baru sahaja membinanya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The step count comes from [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), the fermionic counterpart of the qubit-level formula used as the baseline earlier. Applied to the whole grouped operator before the decomposition, its repetition cycles between the four flow sets and the diagonal group instead of within any one of them:\n"
msgstr "Bilangan langkah datang daripada [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\"), padanan fermion bagi formula peringkat qubit yang digunakan sebagai garis dasar sebelum ini. Dikenakan pada keseluruhan operator berkumpulan sebelum penguraian, ulangannya berkitar antara empat set aliran dan kumpulan pepenjuru dan bukannya di dalam mana-mana satu daripadanya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The fidelity climbs monotonically toward one as the steps shorten, which is the behavior a product formula must show. Shortening the steps is only one of the two knobs; [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") trades them against each other at a higher order, as [Synthesize an Evolution gate in fermionic space](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation) measures.\n"
msgstr "Kesetiaan meningkat secara monotonik ke arah satu apabila langkah memendek, iaitu tingkah laku yang mesti ditunjukkan oleh formula hasil darab. Memendekkan langkah hanyalah satu daripada dua tombol; [`FermionicSuzukiTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-suzuki-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicSuzukiTrotter\") menukar ganti keduanya pada peringkat yang lebih tinggi, seperti yang diukur oleh [Sintesis gate Evolution dalam ruang fermion](fermionic-synthesis#fermionic-synthesis-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A single step of this Hamiltonian at $t = 1$ is a poor approximation (the four hopping sets and the interaction do not commute) so the first row is far from one, and that is the point: the convergence is what confirms the construction, not any single row.\n"
msgstr "Satu langkah Hamiltonian ini pada $t = 1$ ialah penghampiran yang lemah (empat set lompatan dan interaksi tidak kalis tukar tertib) jadi baris pertama jauh daripada satu, dan itulah maksudnya: penumpuanlah yang mengesahkan binaan itu, bukan mana-mana satu baris.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Each factor of the schedule spans every mode of this lattice, so narrowing a factor to its support is a no-op here and the absolute qubit indices `FlowSetSynthesis` matches on are unchanged. A synthesis written for an operator whose groups touch only part of the register would have to account for that relabeling.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Setiap faktor jadual merangkumi setiap mod kekisi ini, jadi mengecilkan faktor kepada sokongannya tidak melakukan apa-apa di sini dan indeks qubit mutlak yang dipadankan oleh `FlowSetSynthesis` tidak berubah. Sintesis yang ditulis untuk operator yang kumpulannya hanya menyentuh sebahagian daftar perlu mengambil kira pelabelan semula itu.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "What to take away {#what-to-take-away}"
msgstr "Apa yang perlu diambil {#what-to-take-away}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two dimensions changes the bookkeeping, not the recipe.** Every ingredient from the 1D guide carries over unmodified: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") for the grouping, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") for the encoding, [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") for the mismatched register, and [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") to wire it into the transpiler. What grew is the number of cases inside each.\n"
msgstr "**Dua dimensi mengubah pengurusan butiran, bukan resipinya.** Setiap bahan daripada panduan 1D terbawa tanpa diubah: [`groups`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-transfer-vertex-operator#qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups \"qiskit_fermions.operators.TransferVertexOperator.groups\") untuk pengumpulan, [`map_transfer_vertex_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/mappers-map-transfer-vertex-generators#qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators \"qiskit_fermions.mappers.map_transfer_vertex_generators\") untuk pengekodan, [`CustomF2QLayout`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-custom-f-2-q-layout#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.CustomF2QLayout\") untuk daftar yang tidak sepadan, dan [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_fermions.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\") untuk menyambungkannya ke dalam transpiler. Yang bertambah ialah bilangan kes di dalam setiap satu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Disjointness is what makes 2D constant-depth.** A flow set decomposes into vertex-disjoint lines, so its Cliffords are emitted in parallel and share two two-qubit layers no matter how large the lattice is. Four flow sets and a diagonal group then give a fixed budget: here $16$ for the four flow sets plus $8$ for the diagonal interaction group.\n"
msgstr "**Keterpisahan itulah yang menjadikan 2D berkedalaman malar.** Satu set aliran terurai kepada garisan bercerai bucu, jadi Clifford-nya dikeluarkan secara selari dan berkongsi dua lapisan dua-qubit tidak kira betapa besar kekisinya. Empat set aliran dan satu kumpulan pepenjuru kemudian memberikan belanjawan tetap: di sini $16$ untuk empat set aliran ditambah $8$ untuk kumpulan interaksi pepenjuru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Each orientation is its own Pauli shape.** $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$ turns `XXZ` into `YYZ` and `XYXY` into `YXXY`, so the four flow sets need four Cliffords. Assuming that one Clifford covers both orientations of an axis is the easiest way to get a 2D flow-set synthesis wrong.\n"
msgstr "**Setiap orientasi ialah bentuk Pauli tersendiri.** $T_{kj} = -V_j V_k T_{jk}$ menukar `XXZ` kepada `YYZ` dan `XYXY` kepada `YXXY`, jadi empat set aliran memerlukan empat Clifford. Menganggap bahawa satu Clifford meliputi kedua-dua orientasi sesuatu paksi ialah cara paling mudah untuk tersilap dalam sintesis set aliran 2D.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Read supports off the conjugation.** In 1D, one `CZ` brickwork gives the images in closed form. In 2D there is no such formula, and column lines have non-contiguous ancillas, so a hand-derived guess at where each term lands is fragile. Conjugating and inspecting the result costs one [`Clifford`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Clifford) construction and cannot be wrong; it also means an equally valid Clifford that lands the terms elsewhere keeps working.\n"
msgstr "**Baca sokongan daripada konjugasi.** Dalam 1D, satu bata `CZ` memberikan imej dalam bentuk tertutup. Dalam 2D tiada formula sedemikian, dan garisan lajur mempunyai ancilla yang tidak bersebelahan, jadi tekaan terbitan tangan tentang tempat setiap sebutan mendarat adalah rapuh. Mengkonjugasi dan memeriksa hasilnya hanya memerlukan satu binaan [`Clifford`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Clifford) dan tidak mungkin salah; ia juga bermakna Clifford yang sama sah yang mendaratkan sebutan di tempat lain terus berfungsi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Let the grouping do the sorting.** Because [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") splits itself per group, the synthesis is handed one flow set at a time and never has to re-derive the partition: it reads one Pauli shape off the first term and picks the matching Clifford. Assuming that, and raising when it does not hold, is what keeps `synthesize` short.\n"
msgstr "**Biarkan pengumpulan membuat pengisihan.** Oleh kerana [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.Evolution\") memecahkan dirinya mengikut kumpulan, sintesis diserahkan satu set aliran pada satu masa dan tidak perlu memperoleh semula pembahagian: ia membaca satu bentuk Pauli daripada sebutan pertama dan memilih Clifford yang sepadan. Mengandaikan itu, dan menimbulkan ralat apabila ia tidak benar, itulah yang memastikan `synthesize` ringkas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The step count sits above the split.** The synthesis here sees one flow set per gate, so it cannot subdivide the evolution across the sets. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") does that in fermionic space, before the decomposition, which is what makes a convergence test possible at all.\n"
msgstr "**Bilangan langkah terletak di atas pemisahan.** Sintesis di sini melihat satu set aliran bagi setiap gate, jadi ia tidak dapat membahagikan evolusi merentasi set. [`FermionicLieTrotter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/circuit-library-synthesis-fermionic-lie-trotter#qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter \"qiskit_fermions.circuit.library.synthesis.FermionicLieTrotter\") melakukannya dalam ruang fermion, sebelum penguraian, yang menjadikan ujian penumpuan mungkin sama sekali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Verify on the subspace.** A $2N$-qubit encoding of $N$ modes is faithful only where the stabilizers say it is. Because VC keeps $V_j = Z_j$, the cheapest reliable check is to project a product state and compare densities: no intertwiner and no spectral matching, which is unreliable when the restricted Hamiltonian is degenerate.\n"
msgstr "**Sahkan pada subruang.** Pengekodan $2N$ qubit bagi $N$ mod hanya setia di tempat penstabil mengatakan ia setia. Oleh kerana VC mengekalkan $V_j = Z_j$, semakan boleh dipercayai yang paling murah ialah mengunjurkan keadaan hasil darab dan membandingkan ketumpatan: tiada pengaitan dan tiada padanan spektrum, yang tidak boleh dipercayai apabila Hamiltonian terhad adalah merosot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The encoded Hamiltonian commutes with the stabilizers, so the projection only has to be applied to the initial state. The evolution preserves the subspace by itself. On real hardware this is also what makes the encoding useful as an error-detection resource: the stabilizers can be measured.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Nota\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  Hamiltonian terkod kalis tukar tertib dengan penstabil, jadi unjuran hanya perlu dikenakan pada keadaan awal. Evolusi memelihara subruang dengan sendirinya. Pada perkakasan sebenar, ini juga yang menjadikan pengekodan berguna sebagai sumber pengesanan ralat: penstabil boleh diukur.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next {#next}"
msgstr "Seterusnya {#next}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two directions extend what is above, and both are changes of ingredient rather than of method. The first is the encoding: Verstraete-Cirac was chosen here because Ref. <span id=\"id15\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) gives its diagonalizing Cliffords in closed form, but Derby-Klassen spends one ancilla per odd plaquette instead of one per site, for a qubit-to-mode ratio of $3/2$ rather than $2$. Its transfer operators have different Pauli shapes, so a port amounts to rewriting the encoding function of [step 3](#flowsets-2d-encoding) and finding the Clifford for each new shape; the grouping, the layout, and the synthesis scaffolding carry over untouched.\n"
msgstr "Dua arah memanjangkan apa yang di atas, dan kedua-duanya ialah perubahan bahan dan bukan kaedah. Yang pertama ialah pengekodan: Verstraete-Cirac dipilih di sini kerana Rujukan <span id=\"id15\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) memberikan Clifford pendiagonalannya dalam bentuk tertutup, tetapi Derby-Klassen menggunakan satu ancilla bagi setiap plakuet ganjil dan bukan satu bagi setiap tapak, untuk nisbah qubit-ke-mod $3/2$ dan bukan $2$. Operator pindahannya mempunyai bentuk Pauli yang berbeza, jadi pemindahan bermaksud menulis semula fungsi pengekodan [langkah 3](#flowsets-2d-encoding) dan mencari Clifford bagi setiap bentuk baharu; pengumpulan, susun atur, dan perancah sintesis terbawa tanpa disentuh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second is the lattice itself. Everything here assumes open boundaries and a single fermionic species. Periodic boundaries close each line into a cycle: the arrows still all commute, since each meets the next head-to-tail, but the two Clifford shapes of [step 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) are built for a line with endpoints. A cycle of $L$ sites carries $L$ bonds per orientation where a line carries $L - 1$, so the wrap-around bond has no place in the construction and needs handling of its own. A spinful model is easier: it doubles the register and adds on-site interaction terms to the diagonal group, without touching the flow sets. Neither disturbs the constant-depth argument, but both change the bookkeeping, which, as the first takeaway says, is the part that two dimensions makes bigger.\n"
msgstr "Yang kedua ialah kekisi itu sendiri. Segala-galanya di sini mengandaikan sempadan terbuka dan satu spesies fermion. Sempadan berkala menutup setiap garisan menjadi kitaran: anak panah masih semuanya kalis tukar tertib, kerana setiap satu bertemu yang seterusnya kepala-ke-ekor, tetapi dua bentuk Clifford [langkah 5](#flowsets-2d-synthesis) dibina untuk garisan berhujung. Kitaran $L$ tapak membawa $L$ ikatan bagi setiap orientasi manakala garisan membawa $L - 1$, jadi ikatan lilitan tidak mempunyai tempat dalam binaan dan memerlukan pengendalian tersendiri. Model berspin lebih mudah: ia menggandakan daftar dan menambah sebutan interaksi atas-tapak pada kumpulan pepenjuru, tanpa menyentuh set aliran. Tiada satu pun mengganggu hujah kedalaman malar, tetapi kedua-duanya mengubah pengurusan butiran, yang, seperti dikatakan oleh pengajaran pertama, ialah bahagian yang dibesarkan oleh dua dimensi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Important\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Hardware connectivity is not addressed here.** Every circuit above is built on an abstract register where any pair of qubits can interact, and the reported depths are counted in that setting. Real devices have a restricted coupling map, and mapping this encoding onto one is a substantial problem in its own right: the VC register is a $2N$-qubit graph whose gates run between a site and its own ancilla, between neighboring sites and between neighboring ancillas, so a layout has to keep all three kinds of pairs adjacent simultaneously. If it cannot, the transpiler inserts `SWAP` gates, and the layers they add are what the constant-depth construction was buying back. Ref.   <span id=\"id16\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) likewise quotes its depth figure under an assumed square connectivity graph with `CX` as the only native entangler. Finding good layouts and routing strategies for local encodings on a given device topology is beyond this guide’s scope.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Penting\" type=\"danger\">\n"
"  **Kesambungan perkakasan tidak dibincangkan di sini.** Setiap litar di atas dibina pada daftar abstrak yang mana-mana pasangan qubit boleh berinteraksi, dan kedalaman yang dilaporkan dikira dalam keadaan itu. Peranti sebenar mempunyai peta gandingan yang terhad, dan memetakan pengekodan ini ke atasnya ialah masalah besar tersendiri: daftar VC ialah graf $2N$ qubit yang gate-nya berjalan antara satu tapak dan ancillanya sendiri, antara tapak berjiran dan antara ancilla berjiran, jadi susun atur mesti mengekalkan ketiga-tiga jenis pasangan itu bersebelahan serentak. Jika tidak boleh, transpiler memasukkan gate `SWAP`, dan lapisan yang ditambahnya ialah apa yang dibeli semula oleh binaan kedalaman malar. Rujukan   <span id=\"id16\" />[\\[1\\]](#id17) juga memetik angka kedalamannya di bawah graf kesambungan segi empat sama yang diandaikan dengan `CX` sebagai satu-satunya pengikat asli. Mencari susun atur dan strategi penghalaan yang baik bagi pengekodan setempat pada topologi peranti tertentu adalah di luar skop panduan ini.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

